From c8ce46f58e861fbcbbb1857a64827eb423135dc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luissalet <luismasc16@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 01:59:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/36] Send the sampler parameters the image server actually
 reads

The runtime parses far more of a generation request than the studio was
sending. Everything added here was checked against
SDGenerationParams::from_json_str in examples/common/common.cpp at the
pinned commit, and cross-checked against make_img_gen_defaults_json in
examples/server/routes_sdcpp.cpp, which is the server's own account of
the same schema.

New on the wire: clip_skip, sample_params.{eta, flow_shift,
shifted_timestep, custom_sigmas, extra_sample_args},
guidance.{img_cfg, slg{layers, layer_start, layer_end, scale}},
hires.{target_width, target_height, custom_sigmas}, vae_tiling_params
and cache_mode/cache_option.

Three traps the source settled, each of which would have produced a
request that succeeded while ignoring the setting:

- hires takes target_width/target_height, not the CLI's target_w/target_h.
- eta and flow_shift live inside sample_params; at the top level nothing
  reads them.
- extra_sample_args is a key=value STRING, not an object, so Adaptive
  Projected Guidance is serialised rather than nested.

ADetailer, IP-Adapter and guidance_schedule are NOT sent: none of those
strings occurs anywhere in the runtime's source at this commit, so the
server would have accepted the keys and done nothing with them.

Steps now clamp to 100 rather than 150 because routes_sdcpp.cpp resolves
requests with strict = true, which clamps sample_steps to 1..100. Asking
for 150 and recording 150 described a picture the runtime made with 100.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
